.TH FAAR 1 "October 2026" "FAAR 3.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
faar \- Freeware Advanced Audio Resampler
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B faar
[\fIoptions\fR] \fIinput\fR \fIoutput\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B faar
is a command-line tool for digital audio sample rate conversion using the staged CPU backend selected by default. It provides linear-phase filtering and optional TPDF dithering with high-pass noise shaping. Rejection, transition bandwidth, memory use, and CPU cost depend on the quality preset and conversion ratio.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-\-rate " " \fIHz\fR
Set target output sampling rate in Hz (e.g. 48000, 44100, 32000). Required.
.TP
.BR \-\-quality " " \fIpreset\fR
Set DSP filter quality preset: \fBfast\fR, \fBgood\fR (default), or \fBhigh\fR. Filter plans depend on the selected backend and conversion rates.
.TP
.BR \-\-boundary " " \fImode\fR
Select endpoint extension for each input stream: \fBhold\fR (default) continues the first and last sample; \fBzero\fR uses silence outside the stream. HOLD avoids a forced step to silence at nonzero endpoints, but independent files still start separate sample clocks. Use one continuous stream when track-to-track clock continuity is required.
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-channels " " \fInum\fR
Set audio channel count for raw PCM input streams [default: 2].
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-format " " \fIfmt\fR
Set raw PCM sample format: \fBf32le\fR (default), \fBs16le\fR, or \fBs24le\fR.
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-dither " " \fItype\fR
Set dithering mode for integer format output: \fBnone\fR (default), \fBtpdf\fR (triangular dither), or \fBshaped\fR (TPDF dither with high-pass noise shaping).
.TP
.BR \-\-decimate
Force multi-stage decimation cascade for large downsampling ratios.
.TP
.BR \-\-ignorelength
Ignore the WAV data length in the input header and read until end-of-file.
.TP
.BR \-v " " \fIlevel\fR
Set verbosity level (\fB\-v0\fR is quiet mode) [default: 1].
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-output " " \fIpath\fR
Specify output file path (use \fB\-\fR for stdout).
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Display command usage guide and exit.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Resample a 96 kHz WAV file to 48 kHz WAV:
.B faar -r 48000 input_96k.wav output_48k.wav
.TP
Resample with High Quality and TPDF dithering to 16-bit WAV in quiet mode:
.B faar -r 48000 --quality high -d tpdf -f s16le -v0 input.wav output.wav
.TP
Stream raw float PCM through a shell pipeline:
.B cat input.raw | faar -r 48000 -c 2 -f f32le - - | aplay -f S16_LE -r 48000
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR faac (1),
.BR faam (1)
